       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin. At that level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially. Kidney and liver function are normal, so nothing in the patient's profile justifies going above the limit.\n\nHere are some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max dose.\n- **1700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg to 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is a typical starting or maintenance range.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is intended. If it is, please give me a reason to put in the order note. I'll enter the order once I have that."
