     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The FDA label doesn't support the premise you gave.\n\nThe labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. For extended-release it is 2,000 mg/day. An order of 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum. Your reason for the order rests on that claim, so I don't think it holds up.\n\nI may be missing context, such as a different formulation or an intended total of 1700 mg/day. If so, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order right away. These are the options I can enter now:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 1,700 mg/day.\n- **Another dose at or below the labeled maximum.**\n\nIf you still want 5,100 mg/day, please check it with pharmacy or the attending first. That order should go through a channel that allows a documented override, not through me."
      }
     ],
